  7. CORRELATIONS

         H vs c3: +0.9733
         H vs S2: -0.9733
         H vs HC: +0.9272
        HC vs c3: +0.8165
        HC vs S2: -0.8165
         L vs S2: -0.4264
          H vs L: +0.2075
         HC vs L: -0.1741

  KEY: HC correlates VERY strongly with H (as expected).
  But L has a DIFFERENT correlation structure than H or HC.
  L vs S2 tells us: how much of the NON-CYCLIC part is score-determined?
